; idxgrid_intermediate_overflow: the product row * cols leaves the signed
; 64-bit range while the final index lands back inside it.
;
; row = 2^62, col = -1, cols = 2. row * cols = 2^63 is not representable;
; row * cols + col = 2^63 - 1 = i64::MAX is. A VM that computes in a wider
; type and range-checks only the pushed result accepts this program and
; pushes i64::MAX. Per spec/xqvm/SPEC.md every i64 operation the VM
; performs on a program's behalf is range-checked, intermediates included,
; so the program must fault.
;
; Neither IDXGRID nor IDXTRIU had a vector anywhere before this pair.

PUSH 4611686018427387904   ; row
PUSH -1                    ; col
PUSH 2                     ; cols
IDXGRID
HALT
